# Editor: variable and parameter names

Apply when writing or editing Vue / TypeScript under `editor/`.

## Prefer full words over abbreviations

- Avoid telegram names (`el`, `cfg`, `msg`, ambiguous `id`).
- Spell out: `entityId`, `screenId`, `tileIndex`, `paletteRole`.
- In multi-line callbacks, name parameters (`tile =>`, `node =>`), not bare `it`-style opacity.

## Leave alone

- Vue `props` and JSON keys that match the server/layout API.
- Serialized field names (`w`, `h`, theme id `rpi`) unless a protocol migration is explicit.

## Lint

- Prefer fixing issues so `npm run lint` stays green.
- Use Prettier via `npm run format`; do not fight `eslint-config-prettier`.
